<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13367"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 3:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting that Rader plead not guilty, but not suprised.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13367-->
<!--Post: 13368--><!--Time: 1115158795-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13368"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 3:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A psychopath enjoys retaining control and Rader will not relinquish it during the trial. It seems his decision to plea not guilty may be motivated by the desire to inflict pain and suffering on the families of his victims. He will most probably proclaim his innocence and argue the physical evidence and biological evidence may be degraded and too old. Rader may suggest he is also a victim of the Wichita Police Department&#39;s attempt to solve this criminal case at any cost. Rader is obsessed with maintaining the facade of respectability while taunting and manipulating the judiciary, media and the public. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13368-->
<!--Post: 13371--><!--Time: 1115162585-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13371"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 4:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy, <BR> <BR>This decision to plead innocent surprises me as I thought that Rader would use the trial to go for the shock and awe campaign.  .  .   <BR> <BR>I thought Rader would revel in describing his crimes, scaring people, and rubbing it in one last time. <BR> <BR>What scares me is if this is a prelude to a challenge of the DNA evidence quality and purity. If the DNA evidence can be overturned has Rader been implicated in any other way ??? <BR> <BR>If not he is looking for an acquittal and that is frightening.  .  .   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13371-->
<!--Post: 13405--><!--Time: 1115219500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13405"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 8:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Tac, remember the day he was arrested.  I am going to go back and check the articles but I definetly remember it was stated that Rader had &#34;confessed&#34; - so something&#39;s gotta be up with that confession.  Prof Phoenix...do you know?  Rocky ? <BR>Anyone remeber this. <BR>I am also afraid that some of the DNA may be to old...I am afraid of an insanity plea...I am afraid this demon @&#42;&#42; will get off period...But I feel confident in Nola...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13405-->
<!--Post: 13426--><!--Time: 1115257031-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13426"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It seems Dennis Rader believes the degraded biological evidence can assist his claim of innocence. Rader is a sadistic psychopath who seems determined to convince the jury he was and remains a respectable and valuable member of the community. It seems Rader may use manipulation. He most probably will express revulsion at the brutality of the 10 murders during the trial and insist he was not capable of committing them. He was a loving husband and father not a sadistic serial murderer. It would provide him with greater satisfaction than admitting to the murders and describing his violent sexual fantasies. The opportunity to avoid punishment and undermine the Wichita Police investigation seems to be an incentive he cannot resist.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13426-->
<!--Post: 13516--><!--Time: 1115439173-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13516"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, May 06, 2005 - 9:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Else: <BR> <BR>I recall that he was arrested mid-day and taken to the Wichita FBI office for interrogation.  He was given a cot to sleep on, and spent the night  at their office. When a defendant invokes his right to silence under Miranda the cops back off.  The amount of time he spent at the FBI office is a VERY strong indication that he confessed. <BR> <BR>The confession issues that are clearly present are: <BR> <BR>1.  He has a mental disorder which makes it more difficult to prove lack of coercion. <BR> <BR>2.  The cops would not let an attorney &#40;hired by the family&#41; talk to him. <BR> <BR>3.  It lasted a long time. <BR> <BR>4.  and a potential issue: if he detaches from reality under stress, &#40;DID&#41; was this a voluntary statement? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m confident that 1, 2, and 3 are present.  4. depends on the interplay between the insanity defense and the content of a motion to supress his statements. <BR> <BR>To be admissable, a confession must be voluntary, and if made while in custody, must follow a &#34;knowing and intelligent waiver&#34; of the right to counsel and the right to remain silent.  Miranda warnings must be given before the waiver and confession.  This is HIGHLY simplified, but I don&#39;t know enough of the specifics to get into more detail yet.  <BR> <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13516-->
<!--Post: 13539--><!--Time: 1115584711-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13539"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 08, 2005 - 1:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Phx <BR> <BR>Solid information. It seems obvious that a lawyer bent Rader&#39;s ear with the idea that the DNA evidence is the weak link.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Frankly it amazes me that our &#34;covert&#34; govt agencys, you know the ones not on the books that don&#39;t exist, employing the many &#34;spooks&#34; aka &#34;ghosts&#34; can and do travel thousands of miles to Outer BuHeefellow to &#34;eliminate&#34; a threat. Yet those same boys in black can&#39;t &#34;eliminate&#34; Rader if he walks away from this mess ?????? <BR> <BR>If they can let Carlos Lehder operate outside jail for decades now why can&#39;t we just put a bullet in it and be done with it ??? <BR> <BR>Citizens for rightgeous revenge unite.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13539-->
<!--Post: 13547--><!--Time: 1115650253-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13547"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 7:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not surprised that Rader plead not guilty. In all actuality, he didn&#39;t plead anything, he stood silent when asked for his plea. That said to me that he&#39;s guilty, but at the same time, couldn&#39;t bring his coward self to lie and plea not guilty. I don&#39;t know if I&#39;m right in this, but look at it this way. He has nothing to lose to go ahead and try to plead not guilty. He doesn&#39;t face the death penalty if the trial doesn&#39;t pan out in his favor, so if there is some way out in doing this &#40;bad DNA, insanity defense, mistrial, ETC&#41;, what&#39;s the harm to the bast&#42;&#42;d?  <BR> <BR>&#42;I have the utmost faith in the DNA evidence. <BR> <BR>&#42;I also highly doubt that a insanity defense will work out. He was a compliance officer. He has a military background. He was a big presence in his church.  <BR> <BR>&#42; In all of that stuff taken from his home, I am sure there is enough evidence there to choke an army or horses!  <BR> <BR>&#42; His wife knows what&#39;s up. If my husband was the one picked up and is believed to be BTK, if I had an ounce of thought of his innocence &#40;this includes if I thought he did it, but wasn&#39;t mentally able to know right from wrong&#41; , I would stand by him, not try to get away from him.  <BR> <BR>If he were, by some act of GOD, to be aquitted, you know he would have to get into hiding.  <BR> <BR>He&#39;ll get his. Just my thoughts on the matter.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13547-->
<!--Post: 13551--><!--Time: 1115666439-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13551"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 12:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beck, I so agree with you.  Expecially, the part about his &#34;wife&#34;.  IF she felt he was &#34;not guilty&#34; she would stand by him...I think she also knows and has known that there was something really wrong...she is hiding...won&#39;t talk to him...no support whatsoever...even the rumors about divorce. <BR>If he was such the loving husband, father, and Christian do-gooder...why isn&#39;t the whole ding dang family surrounding him??????????e<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13551-->
<!--Post: 13554--><!--Time: 1115672596-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13554"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, May 09, 2005 - 2:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the wife knew in advance or had suspicions why didn&#39;t she go to the police with them ? She could have been charged as an accessory otherwise...and if the daughter does scream at night what else did denny do that we don&#39;t know about ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
